A while back there were a series of posts on getting rid of items.
 
If you have been in a dungeon for quite a while you can get fed up
with all the junk around and checking the items left by a deceased
monster for that potion/scroll you are after is a pain.

I propose two new commands, Trash used on a pile of objects  would
give a message like 
"There are several items here, trash what? [)(!? Aa]"
then
"8 poisoned orcish arrows (ynaq) ?"

Of course some safe guards might be needed so Artifacts  dont  get
trashed by accident.  The only slight real advantage it gives  the
player is that monsters wont have as much armour/weapons to pickup
and wear and be honest, how much difference does that make to you?

Second There could be a Junklist option, simply a  list  of  items
you have no interest in. After monsters die any items in the  list
simply disappear in a puff of smoke.

If you want to restrict such a junk list simply make a 'junk item'
scroll. Cursed ones would junk a random item ("Potions of healing
will no longer be found ...") while blessed ones  would  be  like
blessed identify scrolls and allow several items to be junked.




